Abstracts
                           Scientific articles usually provide an abstract which is a brief
                           overview/summary of their core topics, or arguments. The
                           next example demonstrates typesetting an abstract using
                           LATEX’s abstract environment:

                             \documentclass{article}
                             \begin{document}
                             \begin{abstract}
                             This is a simple paragraph at the beginning of
                             the
                             document. A brief introduction about the main
                             subject.
                             \end{abstract}
                             \end{document}
